WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.540
Poisoning can happen in many ways, whether something is swallowed, breathed in, or even

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:09.040
just touches the skin or eyes.

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:13.800
You might notice a wide range of symptoms, such as dizziness, a headache, difficulty

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:16.700
breathing, or even nausea and vomiting.

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:19.600
Your first priority is always scene safety.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:24.240
If you see spilled or leaking containers, do not approach the area, and make sure to

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:26.620
tell others to stay away as well.

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:31.400
When providing care, the person's level of consciousness determines your next move.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:37.980
If they are alert and stable, your first call should be to Poison Control at 1-800-222-1222.

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:45.459
However, if they are not alert or appear unstable, call 911 immediately and be prepared to perform

00:00:45.459 --> 00:00:47.900
CPR if they stop breathing.

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:51.740
For inhaled poisons, move the person to fresh air right away.

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:56.020
And for chemical burns on the skin, remember to rinse the affected area with clean water

00:00:56.259 --> 00:00:57.860
for at least 15 minutes.

00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:02.639
If you are dealing with poison oak, ivy, or sumac, your goal is to remove the oils by

00:01:02.639 --> 00:01:07.860
taking off any contaminated clothing and washing the skin thoroughly with soap and water.

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:11.980
You can use over-the-counter medications for the itch, but see a healthcare professional

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:13.379
if it gets worse.

00:01:13.379 --> 00:01:18.500
In many environments, you can also find a Safety Data Sheet, or SDS, which provides

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:21.699
specific first aid information for different poisons.

00:01:21.739 --> 00:01:24.620
Before moving on, I want you to consider this question.

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:28.980
If a child swallowed a household cleaner but is currently alert and talking, what would

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:30.500
be your very first phone call?

